  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Displaced Talent for Europe 2.0</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This new project, Displaced Talent for Europe 2.0 (DT4E 2.0) will be a follow-up to DT4E. The project will scale up, in numerical and geographical terms, complementary labour pathways to the EU in both their traditional and hybrid forms, as developed and piloted in DT4E. DT4E 2.0 will further develop and scale up (&#x201c;deepen&#x201d;) the pathway already set up in BE (&#x201c;frontrunner&#x201d;) and to replicate (&#x201c;broaden&#x201d;) this model and open new complementary pathways to FR and SK, &#x201c;newcomers&#x201d; which currently do not have any initiative in place. In parallel, DT4E 2.0 will expand the target pool of displaced talent and potentially include other refugee-hosting countries. The project will enable people in need of international protection in JD and LB to connect with employers in BE, FR and SK, with the ultimate goal of sustainably integrating the labour market in those countries. The project aims at strengthening EU countries&#x2019; capacities to establish and implement complementary pathways for displaced talents and will contribute to a higher number of displaced people gaining access to durable solutions whilst addressing labour shortages in the EU.</narrative>
  </description>
